<onlyinclude>'''Semiotics''' is the study of signs and how they represent or communicate something. Words, images, gestures and other phenomena can function as signs when interpreted in a context. A road sign can instruct a driver even though the physical shape is not itself the action it represents.

== Explanation ==
Charles Sanders Peirce described a relation among sign, object and interpretant. Ferdinand de Saussure emphasized the relation between a signifier and signified in language. These influential traditions differ; neither implies that every sign has only one fixed meaning independent of context.

